      {
        "text": "What does \":%norm\" do in vim?"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "role": "model",
    "parts": [
      {
        "thoughtSignature": "",
        "text": "In Vim, `:%norm` executes a sequence of Normal mode commands for every line in the file.\n\nHere's a breakdown:\n\n*   `:` Enters Command-line mode.\n*   `%` Is a range that specifies all lines in the file.\n*   `norm` Is the command that executes the following characters as if they were typed in Normal mode.\n\n**Example:**\n\nIf you run `:%norm A;`, Vim will go to every line (`%`), and for each one, it will execute the Normal mode command `A;`. The `A` command moves the cursor to the end of the line and enters Insert mode, `;` types a semicolon, and the command implicitly exits Insert mode for the next line.\n\nThe result is that a semicolon is appended to every line in the file."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "parts": [
      {
        "text": "Nice! So what should \n\n```vim\n:%norm Ihttps://www.youtube.com/@^[A/\n```\n\ndo?"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "role": "model",
    "parts": [
      {
        "thoughtSignature": "",
        "text": "That command is designed to wrap each line in the file with a YouTube channel URL structure.\n\nLet's break it down for a single line:\n\n*   `:%norm`: Execute the following Normal mode commands on every line.\n*   `I`: Move to the first non-whitespace character of the line and enter Insert mode.\n*   `https://www.youtube.com/@`: Type this literal string at the beginning of the line.\n*   `^[`: This is the representation of the `Escape` key. It takes you out of Insert mode and back to Normal mode. You would typically type this in the Vim command line by pressing `Ctrl-V` then `Esc`.\n*   `A`: Move to the end of the line and enter Insert mode.\n*   `/`: Type this literal character at the end of the line.\n\n**In practice:**\n\nIf you have a file with a list of YouTube channel handles like this:\n\n```\nMrBeast\nmkbhd\n```\n\nRunning `:%norm Ihttps://www.youtube.com/@^[A/` would transform it into:\n\n```\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@MrBeast/\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@mkbhd/\n```"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "parts": [
      {
        "text": "What about `:%norm gx`"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "role": "model",
    "parts": [
      {
        "thoughtSignature": "",
        "text": "The command `:%norm gx` would attempt to open every line of your file as a URL in your system's default web browser.\n\n*   `:%norm`: Execute the following on every line.\n*   `gx`: This is a Normal mode command that opens the URL found under the cursor in an external application (usually your default browser). When run on a line, it treats the line's content as the URL.\n\n**Warning:**\n\nIf your file has many lines, this command will try to open a new browser tab for **every single line**, which could easily freeze or crash your browser or system. Be very careful when using it on files with more than a few lines."
      }
    ]
  },
